ountry>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUMIKAWA NAOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMADA, KAORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKO, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIMURA, YOSHIHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIDORIKAWA, YOSHIMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMIKAWA, NAOMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thermal recording sheet which has high sensitivity in color development, satisfactory background heat resistance, and a satisfactory background color. The sheet contains a dihydroxydiphenyl sulfone compound represented by general formula (1) as a color developer and a sulfonamide represented by general formula (2). In the formula, R1 and R2 each represents C1-8 alkyl, alkenyl, or halogeno; and p and q each is an integer of 0 to 3. In the formula, R3 represents C1-6 alkyl or electron-attracting group; and n is an integer of 0 to 2.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne une feuille d'enregistrement thermique présentant une bonne sensibilité pour le développement des couleurs, une bonne résistance à la chaleur du fond, et une bonne couleur de fond. La feuille contient, d'une part un composé dihydroxydiphényle-sulfoné représenté par la formule générale (1) et intervenant comme développeur couleurs organique, et d'autre part un sulfonamide représenté par la formule générale (2). Dans ces formules, R1 et R2 sont chacun C1-C8 alkyle, alcényle, ou halogène, "p" et "q" sont chacun un entier de 0 à 3, R3 est C1-C6 alkyle ou un groupe attirant les électrons, et "n" est un entier de 0 à 2.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>